[low, security] git-store/src/main.rs:476-497 (edit_in_editor) — the editor temp file is created at a predictable path in the shared temp dir (git-store-<pid>.json) with std::fs::write, which follows symlinks. A local attacker who can predict the pid can plant a symlink there and have the seed content written through it to a victim-writable path (CWE-377), or pre-populate content the user then edits. Use the tempfile crate (already a workspace dev-dependency) with a randomized name and O_EXCL creation. Two smaller nits in the same function: the file leaks if read_to_string fails after a successful edit, and the 'editor exited without saving' message is wrong — a nonzero exit doesn't mean nothing was saved.
